' SOUNDING
' An original game by Claude (an AI made by Anthropic) for Amy Studio and
' Amy Bienvenu, 2026. The echolocation look (a dark screen where only the
' surfaces a sound touches light up) was Amy's idea.
'
' A young bat is lost deep underground, too young to know the way. Bats
' find their way in the dark by clicking and listening, and so do you: press the button
' to click, and the sound spreads through the open cave (around corners,
' never through rock), lighting the rock it touches for a moment before
' it fades back to black. Find the way out of twelve caves. Moths glow when a
' click finds them; cave snakes hear your clicks and come to where you
' made them. Water drips make their own small sounds, and those light the
' rock too.
'
' How the wave works: each click is a flood through open air, one layer of
' cells a frame (wave.asm). Rock beside the air it reaches is drawn with
' the edge for its open sides. Each click draws with one of four tile
' sets, and the set fades by rewriting only its colours, so a click glows
' and darkens smoothly with nothing redrawn and nothing flashing.
'
' House rules kept: joystick only; text in columns 2-29 and rows 1-22
' (the caves are columns 2-29, rows 2-22); tiles at 128 and up; a title
' tune that plays once (Amy's play song ... once); a credits page; the
' frame loop is protected from the NMI and every screen is drawn with the
' NMI off after a wait.

